-- Brand stories for Compadres Cigars (from compadrescigars.com "About Us") and Sugarhill (replaces the "Draft copy" placeholder).
-- Idempotent; only fills an empty Compadres story or the Sugarhill placeholder, so copy edited in the admin is left alone.
update brands set story = E'Compadres Cigars are hand made in Tamboril, Dominican Republic, the world capital of cigars. Each cigar is made with hand-selected tobacco, free of chemicals and dyes, and carefully inspected for the finest result.\n\nCompadres Cigars is a division of GEO Foods, founded by Spencer Woodard, who has spent about 15 years in the agricultural industry, much of it importing and exporting from Latin America. In 2019 GEO Foods opened an office in the Dominican Republic and sent Jose Suarez, a Cuban national from Havana and a lifelong cigar aficionado, to oversee manufacturing and logistics. There he met Frances Santana of Tamboril, and together they created the specialty blends that became the Compadres line.\n\nAfter two years of development and market testing with veteran cigar smokers, Compadres now offers a full line of premium cigars. From the tobacco fields to the finished cigar, every step is closely monitored and done by hand, and the brand is overseen from production through importing and distribution, with offices in Kansas City, Missouri, and Santiago, Dominican Republic.'
where slug = 'compadres-cigars' and (story is null or btrim(story) = '');

update brands set story = E'In 1979, in Englewood, New Jersey, a producer put three young MCs in a studio and changed popular music. “Rapper''s Delight” by the Sugarhill Gang became the first rap single to reach the top 40 of the Billboard Hot 100, peaking at number 36 in January 1980, and it is now counted among the most important rap songs ever recorded.\n\nThe group was assembled by Sylvia Robinson, co-founder of Sugar Hill Records, with Henry “Big Bank Hank” Jackson, Michael “Wonder Mike” Wright and Guy “Master Gee” O''Brien. Both the group and the label take their name from the Sugar Hill neighborhood of Harlem. “Apache” and “8th Wonder” followed, the group reformed in 1994, and in 2019 it marked the 40th anniversary of “Rapper''s Delight” with a world tour.\n\nSugarhill cigars bring that story to the humidor: bold, loud, and made to be shared. Rapper''s Delight is the first release.'
where slug = 'sugarhill' and story like 'Draft copy, pending client approval.%';
